{"canonicalProfile":"counterlab-canonical-json-v1","capsuleId":"sample-proof-leakage-01-v1","entries":[{"byteLength":550,"content":"CounterLab Sample Proof Capsule v1\n\nMode: fixed sample lesson (leakage-01)\nSupport: Verified sample evidence\nIntegrity: SHA-256 hashed, not signed\n\nGPT-5.6, Runtime Codex, and the hosted runner were not called.\nNo learner Prediction, revision, or learner event chain is represented.\nThe confirmed Belief Spec records fixed-fixture author approval, not an observed learner action.\nThe scientific-engine snapshot is reproduction-candidate metadata, not execution or deployment proof.\nLive notebook Proof Capsule v2 remains a separate authority format.\n","contentEncoding":"utf-8","mediaType":"text/plain;charset=utf-8","path":"README.txt","sha256":"e9dfbf76f2da63867ece9f260c714ba4e50f2cb6230f7c9d6d71240a763b70eb"},{"byteLength":3271,"content":"{\"artifactId\":\"artifact_d0e9f3238753f1ca55534446\",\"cells\":[{\"index\":0,\"metricCandidates\":[],\"outputHashes\":[],\"sourceExcerpt\":\"# Customer churn: does 99% mean new-customer generalization? This public sample intentionally uses a row-wise split while retaining `customer_id`.\",\"sourceSha256\":\"209a116d9976e05001b46a3741a321daef5e28df283bd313341875564f97d665\",\"symbols\":[],\"type\":\"markdown\"},{\"executionCount\":1,\"index\":1,\"metricCandidates\":[],\"outputHashes\":[\"799b0dea67c9d8ffb82ec6166155bdeddcb4f27b11d89fd138f25ede0e98b0fd\"],\"sourceExcerpt\":\"from pathlib import Path import pandas as pd data_path = Path('../public/customer_churn.csv') df = pd.read_csv(data_path) df[['customer_id', 'churned']].head()\",\"sourceSha256\":\"acf23811d7e111ee37be71dd4182e90ed69719f090586d66721882ec0f664abf\",\"symbols\":[],\"type\":\"code\"},{\"index\":2,\"metricCandidates\":[],\"outputHashes\":[],\"sourceExcerpt\":\"## Reported evaluation The next cell uses a random row split. Repeated observations from one customer can land on both sides.\",\"sourceSha256\":\"a9461d19533c078644bd72d4f6004b051f9332a9489ba02709927e575869e28f\",\"symbols\":[],\"type\":\"markdown\"},{\"executionCount\":2,\"index\":3,\"metricCandidates\":[{\"name\":\"accuracy\",\"outputIndex\":0,\"value\":0.985},{\"name\":\"roc_auc\",\"outputIndex\":0,\"value\":0.984}],\"outputHashes\":[\"00bad59d595b3f3629337f4a413dfa5c20352aab545a9b8926e271974ecacbf4\",\"7c41918bdb9c57a95d1d91b2576fbfb36ec113784b470d963f392509b6bd5113\"],\"sourceExcerpt\":\"from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression from sklearn.metrics import accuracy_score, roc_auc_score from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline from sklearn.preprocessing impor\",\"sourceSha256\":\"af9b2153da597bd0b7f164e8a05bfbfd1426095481d69abf5387dc61c9b48c87\",\"symbols\":[\"train_test_split\",\"ColumnTransformer\",\"OneHotEncoder\",\"Pipeline\",\"LogisticRegression\",\"accuracy_score\",\"roc_auc_score\"],\"type\":\"code\"},{\"index\":4,\"metricCandidates\":[],\"outputHashes\":[],\"sourceExcerpt\":\"**Learner claim to test:** This result proves the model generalizes to customers it has never seen.\",\"sourceSha256\":\"0ec8bac100acc27b608fe93e584296e8d9f9fa80004238c706d318495ea8b3eb\",\"symbols\":[],\"type\":\"markdown\"}],\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-14T00:00:00.000Z\",\"fileName\":\"customer_churn_leakage.ipynb\",\"fileSha256\":\"d0e9f3238753f1ca55534446d83e36041590f31c607a011def3f1d0db3a5bbc9\",\"nbformat\":4,\"packageHints\":[\"pandas\",\"pathlib\",\"sklearn\"],\"schemaSummary\":{\"entityCandidates\":[\"customer_id\"],\"fields\":[{\"inferredType\":\"categorical\",\"name\":\"observation_id\",\"privacyClass\":\"feature\"},{\"inferredType\":\"categorical\",\"name\":\"customer_id\",\"privacyClass\":\"entity_identifier\"},{\"inferredType\":\"number\",\"name\":\"tenure_months\",\"privacyClass\":\"feature\"},{\"inferredType\":\"number\",\"name\":\"monthly_charges\",\"privacyClass\":\"feature\"},{\"inferredType